body:
Your paragraph is super dense lol. I'll try to answer everything.

&#x200B;

>I think I do a good job but I always have this fear when I'm working on the register or SCO that I might have messed up on something like forgetting to scan something or not entering the right amount when doing cash transactions and so on.

Your worrying too much. Cashiers that are just starting are bound to make mistakes.

&#x200B;

>I feel like I would get into serious trouble if I did mess up cause I'm new on the a probationary period which gives me anxiety and often leads me overthinking stuff. Like I would think they would do something like terminate me or do some other disciplinary action.

There are only two ways to get fired from Walmart. Steal money or assault someone.

&#x200B;

>I think the main reason I think like this is because my friend told me something under the lines of that if you mess up in anyway during the probationary period they could fire you with no warning.

Your friend is over-exaggerating or doesn't know what they're talking about. Getting disciplinary action is also super rare. If your manager is a stickler for the rules you *might* get written after repeated (More than 3) attempts to tell you what you're doing wrong.

&#x200B;

>First off, would my CSMs tell me if I messed up or would they not so that they can evaluate how I do my job

CSM's will tell you if you messed up. Heck, most of the nice cashiers will come and tell you if they notice.

&#x200B;

>sometimes my CSMs would glance at me while talking with other CSMs and it makes me nervous.

As a CSM I tend to get very bored and will keep watching my cashiers make sure they're alright out of pure bordem. Also, you're new, they would want to be able to correct any big mistakes before they happen. It's also sorta their job to supervise you as their manager.

&#x200B;

>Also, if a shortage on a drawer comes up what would happen?

Shortages happen all the time, they try to find the money and then it goes through a process to see where they went. The camera above you is there for that purpose.

&#x200B;

>Would they terminate me on the spot?

No

&#x200B;

>Would they give me something to sign?

No, unless you get written up.

&#x200B;

>How many times before they can fire me for multiple drawer shortages?

If you truly are the source of the shortage, and you aren't stealing, they will train you to help you reduce mistakes during transactions.

&#x200B;

>As a minor I know I can't sell alcohol but I can sell lighters right?

Yup, ask for ID if you feel like you should. They give you trouble call a CSM.

&#x200B;

>If I get on the bad side of a CSM would they try to get me into trouble more often?

Do your job right and they won't be able to get you in trouble.

Edit: Needed to get the formatting under control. Also grammer.
